<title>BELGIUM: SGB sees further rise in profit in 1997.</title>
<headline>SGB sees further rise in profit in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian holding company Societe Generale de Belgique SA (SGB) said on Wednesday it expected profit to continue to increase in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;Consolidated net profit on ordinary activities and net profit will continue to rise in 1997,&quot; it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Net profit on ordinary activities should be boosted further by the continuing steady increase in income from Fortis AG, Generale Bank, Tractebel and Sagem. It said in view of their earnings prospects Union Miniere and Recticel could also make a positive contribution to net profit on ordinary activities in 1997.  </p>
<p>An SGB spokesman said the group expected to book in 1997 a 2.6 billion franc capital gain on the sale of its 10.34 percent stake in France's Accor hotel group earlier this year.</p>
<p>The sale was in line with SGB's strategy of focusing on core shareholdings.</p>
<p>SGB is a unit of French Cie de Suez.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
